{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Visits Vanessa at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "As Cool As a Cucumber"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Phrasal Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A phrasal verb is a phrase formed with a verb + preposition. <br/><br/>The combination of the verb and preposition changes the meaning of the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here are some phrasal verbs related to work:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "to work towards -- to take actions hoping to achieve a specific goal<br/>to come up -- to think of<br/>to go over -- to review, to study<br/>to go along -- to accept, to agree to<br/>to go out -- to leave the house, to go to a place or places in the town or city<br/>to come out -- to join people socially <br/>to come back -- to return to a place<br/>to check out -- to experience for the first time<br/>to make sure -- to verify<br/>to run into -- to meet someone without planning<br/>to set up -- to arrange, to organize<br/>to get along -- to be friendly, enjoy being with someone<br/>to follow up -- to ask questions or make comments after a decision or meeting"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You conjugate phrasal verbs in the same way you conjugate other verbs."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Affirmative Form</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Question Form</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Tense</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I go out on Saturdays.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do you go out on Saturdays?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I am going out this evening.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Are you going out this evening?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I went out last Saturday.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Did you go out last Saturday?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have gone out every Saturday this month. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Have you gone out every Saturday this month?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect tense\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was fun to check out Bistro 88. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Next time I go out with some friends for a meal, we'll come here."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking and Giving Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are several ways to ask for help in English. You can use polite and casual language to do this. Let's look at one particular structure for asking for help."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the structure:<br/>Can/Could + you + show/tell+ me+ Question word"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Can you show me how to make lasagna?<br/>Could you show me where the washrooms are?<br/>Could you tell me what is on the dessert menu?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To give advice, you can use the structure:<br/>Let me show/tell + you + question word"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Let me show you where it is.<br/>Let me tell you what you should do.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you tell me what is the most interesting part of your job?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Could you explain to me how you deal with problems?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "design"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way an object or environment appears, after careful thought and planning"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The food is great and the design is so cool!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "clientele"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the people who purchase goods or services, like meals at a restaurant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our clientele expects great service, so we need to deliver!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to make sure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to verify"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to make sure everyone follows the plan."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to go along"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to accept, to agree to"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sometimes employees don't always go along with the roles they have been assigned to. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to work towards"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take actions with the hope of reaching a specific goal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: After all, we're all working towards the same goal. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le07ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "te